The mayor and council hereby find that:
(1) The Georgia Comprehensive Solid Waste Management Act imposes upon municipalities within the state an obligation to develop and implement plans to reduce, on a per capita basis, the amount of municipal solid waste being received at landfills and other disposal facilities by 25 percent;
(2) In order to achieve compliance and facilitate the stated goals of the Georgia Comprehensive Solid Waste Management Act, the city has heretofore adopted a solid waste management plan establishing procedures for achieving state-mandated waste reduction;
(3) The Georgia Comprehensive Solid Waste Management Act also requires municipalities to update municipal solid waste management plans from time to time, to measure performance, and to implement additional procedures, strategies and methods to reduce solid waste by 25 percent;
(4) Strategies included within the city solid waste management plan include provisions encouraging each applicant for a city land disturbance permit to develop a waste generation analysis and reduction plan for the proposed project;
(5) The city is in the process of updating its solid waste management plan and deems it to be appropriate to implement an ordinance to formalize and establish enforcement procedures requiring the submission of a waste generation analysis and reduction plan for approval as part of the city's plan review process, and to provide procedures to ensure ongoing compliance with approved waste reduction plans; and
(6) The mayor and council find that the adoption of the ordinance from which this chapter is derived is within the basic police powers of the city, and that the provisions contained herein are intended to protect the public health, safety and well-being of city residents, and to protect and enhance the quality of the city's environment in furtherance of a comprehensive statewide program for solid waste management.
